    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why these pages exist",
      "prov:value": "A directory nobody can see is one nobody checks. Measured on this instance,\n2026-09-20: **19 declared subgraphs had no way to look at them**, and the two\nmost depended on were among them — `schemas/`, whose shapes everything else is\nvalidated against, and `library/`, which every knowledge-graph reference to a\nsource resolves *through*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why these pages exist",
      "prov:value": "Bean `2krx` states the rule this is the first half of: **every directory an\ninstance names as a subgraph needs a visualiser, a documentation entry, and a\ngoverning skill.** Three separate requirements, because they fail differently\n— nothing renders it, nothing says what it is for, and nothing an agent can\ninvoke against it. This page is the second of the three for these two graphs;\n[`schema-management`]({{ '/reference/skill-instructions/schema-management.html' | relative_url }}) and\nthe library-ingestion skills are the third."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The relationship diagram",
      "prov:value": "**It is scoped, and refusing is an answer.** The diagram draws the page's scope\nnarrowed by the module filter; above 40 declarations it declines and says to\npick a module. Drawing 812 labelled boxes is the hairball the knowledge-graph\nviewer measured at 1111 nodes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is read-only",
      "prov:value": "Nothing on this page edits an asset. The actions that would write — starting an\ningest from the corpus view, and materialising an entry into a folio of choice\n— are open work, because the write path is a decision the repository owner has\nnot yet made."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "The voices — what each rule cites",
      "prov:value": "A voice is an editorial register asserted by an instance, and this subsystem's\nwhole claim is that it is **auditable rather than asserted**. `check-voices.ts`\nexists because PR #210 shipped three WHO profiles carrying ten plausible rules\neach with `source: null` — and one of those plausible rules asserted the\nopposite of what the WHO Editorial Style Manual says on p14. Every rule now\ncarries the page and the quote.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#210"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The voices — what each rule cites",
      "prov:value": "**Until this page, none of it was readable without opening JSON.** A citation\nthat is only machine-checked is one the reader takes on trust, which is the\nstate the citations were added to end. So the rule row leads with the quote,\nand the citation is the one column that cannot be filtered away. Bean `bu2q`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A declared directory that is not there gets a row",
      "prov:value": "`agent-skills` declares a `voices` graph and ships none. It appears in the\ndirectories table as **declared, not present**, rather than being omitted:\nthose are different facts, and a consumer that scans nothing and reports a\nclean run is the `dh4f` defect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The visualiser rule did not ask for this page",
      "prov:value": "`owesVisualiser` returns false for a `content` kind and `voices` is `content`,\nso `check:subgraph-coverage` never raised a finding for it — exactly as it\nnever raised one for the library. What this page answers is `2krx`'s own\nsentence, *\"a directory nobody can see is one nobody checks\"*, which is a\nreason to build a viewer and not a row in a report."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/subgraph-viewers.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "`docs/` is the same shape, and its subject means something specific",
      "prov:value": "Measured 2026-09-20: only `cat-harness` has a `docs/` directory today, and its\ndeclaration carried `dependents: \"skip\"` — which was exactly what prevented a\ndependent from getting one. Since 2026-09-30 (option A) the field is retired:\nevery instance's existing `docs/` is a **member** of the one declared `docs`\nsubgraph, and `docs` is a `perInstance` kind, so a dependent gets its own.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
